# GI-002, both halves: the shipped asset and its first consumer.
#
# The first block enumerates every git invocation the guard actually
# EXECUTES, with comment lines stripped — the header discusses the
# anti-pattern by name so a whole-file scan would flag the documentation.
# Every surviving query is an index query: --cached for the path list,
# and :0:<path> blob reads for the content. No stash, in any form.
# rev-parse --verify HEAD is a ref-existence check for the unborn-branch
# fallback, not a working-tree read.
#
# The pioneer block is the consumer half (A-034: run tooling, in scope;
# Pioneer PRODUCT code untouched). It lives in its own git repository at
# /Users/rayjanoka/ab/code/pioneer/.claude, so it cannot ride in this
# casting commit and is committed separately there. Its four
# `git diff --name-only HEAD` calls became `git diff --cached
# --name-only`; the exit-0-pass / exit-2-block contract is unchanged.
#
# The registration block matters as much as the query fix: the hook had
# NO Stop entry, so it never ran at all. A correct guard that is never
# invoked is not a guard.

